"""Train four model families and select an ensemble by validation Average Precision.



Python >= 3.10. Install:

&#x20;   python3 -m pip install "numpy>=1.24" "pandas>=2.0" "scipy>=1.10" \\

&#x20;       "scikit-learn>=1.3" "lightgbm>=4.0" "xgboost>=2.0"

Run:

&#x20;   python3 train_channel_model.py --data-dir . --output-dir results_ensemble



The latest cutoff is held out for ensemble selection. Five-fold stratified CV

on earlier rows selects each base configuration and supplies OOF meta-features.

Validation scores are selection scores, not an unbiased generalization estimate.

Repeated channels and temporal overlap may make shuffled inner CV optimistic.

All imputers are fitted inside each fold. No CatBoost or RandomForest is used.

Rank outputs are ranking scores, not calibrated probabilities.

"""



